### Verify the BTP Router with an IAS user token
### Works with VS Code REST Client and compatible .http clients.
### Replace placeholders locally. Never commit secrets, codes, or tokens.

@appUrl = https://<route-from-cf-app>
@iasHost = <tenant>.accounts.ondemand.com
@clientId = <identity-service-clientid>
@clientSecret = <identity-service-clientsecret>
@redirectUri = http://localhost:8080/callback
@authCode = <paste-fresh-authorization-code>

### 1. Public liveness check
GET {{appUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. IAS discovery; verify that issuer and endpoints belong to your tenant
GET https://{{iasHost}}/.well-known/openid-configuration
Accept: application/json

### 3. Open this URL in a browser and sign in
### Add http://localhost:8080/callback to the IAS app's redirect URIs first.
### The callback page may not load; copy the `code` query parameter from its URL.
###
### https://{{iasHost}}/oauth2/authorize?response_type=code&client_id={{clientId}}&redirect_uri=http://localhost:8080/callback&scope=openid%20email%20offline_access

### 4. Exchange the fresh authorization code for an IAS token
# @name token
POST https://{{iasHost}}/oauth2/token
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
Accept: application/json

grant_type=authorization_code&code={{authCode}}&redirect_uri={{redirectUri}}&client_id={{clientId}}&client_secret={{clientSecret}}

### 5. MCP initialize through the default /mcp route
POST {{appUrl}}/mcp
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/json, text/event-stream
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "jsonrpc": "2.0",
  "id": 1,
  "method": "initialize",
  "params": {
    "protocolVersion": "2024-11-05",
    "capabilities": {},
    "clientInfo": {
      "name": "router-verification",
      "version": "1.0"
    }
  }
}

### 6. Optional OData example; enable/configure an /odata route first
### Replace the service path with one exposed by your backend.
GET {{appUrl}}/odata/<SERVICE>/$metadata
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.$.access_token}}
Accept: application/xml
